<h2>1. Our Security Commitment</h2>
<p>We welcome security researchers and ethical hackers to test and report any vulnerabilities discovered within <code>aimadulislam.dpdns.org</code>. We are committed to working constructively with the security community to validate and resolve confirmed issues promptly.</p>

<h2>2. Guidelines for Testing</h2>
<p>To qualify for safe harbor under this policy, security researchers must adhere to the following principles:</p>
<ul>
    <li>Do <strong>NOT</strong> attempt Denial of Service (DoS/DDoS) attacks, brute-force spamming, or social engineering against domain administrators.</li>
    <li>Do <strong>NOT</strong> modify or destroy user data or system integrity.</li>
    <li>Provide detailed proof-of-concept steps to enable verification.</li>
    <li>Allow us reasonable time (up to 30 days) to remediate vulnerabilities before public disclosure.</li>
</ul>

